{
  "_README": "Curated bridge layer for the A-Box builder (scripts/build_abox_experts_problems.py). Maps a NORMALIZED free-text tag (lowercase; / _ - . collapsed to single spaces) found on expert profiles / SME problems to one or more ontology node IDs from data/semiconductor_v0_3.json. This is the auditable, deterministic part of the lossy lift: only terms with a defensible ontology home are listed; genuinely out-of-ontology terms (DRAM, DDR5, FEOL, generic 'materials'/'parts') are intentionally absent and reported as unmatched. Tier-1 (exact lexicon: canonical_name / id-local / synonyms incl. Korean) is applied first; this file is Tier-2. Extend from data/reports/abox_linking_report.json -> top_unmatched.",
  "_format": "<normalized term>: <node_id> | [<node_id>, ...]  — 모든 프로파일에 적용. 프로파일별로 갈라야 하면 {\"expert-tag\": <target|null>, \"patent-text\": <target|null>} 객체를 쓴다 (null = 그 프로파일에서 비활성). 파일을 복제하지 않는다.",
  "_profiles": {
    "expert-tag": "전문가 프로필·SME 문제 태그용 (현행 · 동작 불변 · T3 회귀 금지).",
